    "note": "Acetate-methanogen decay reverted to the ADM1 standard so the plant has a usable healthy point. The FOS/TAC regime is set by the ORGANIC load, not the volume: the load band above is in 'nominal-equivalent m3/d' (the degradable-COD load the nominal mix delivers at that volume). See feed_composition."
  },
  "feed_composition": {
    "note": "The substrate mix varies per phase (a load change may also change which substrates are fed) and differs per series. To keep the modes invariant to the mix, the load is steered as an organic (degradable-COD) load: for each phase the volumetric flows are scaled so the COD load equals the target, since the substrates differ ~7x in COD per m3 (slurry weakest, cereal silage and maize strongest). feed_true holds the actual volumetric flows [m3/d].",
    "active_substrates_per_phase": "2-5 (biased to 4-5)",
    "keep_mix_at_switch_prob": 0.4,
    "volume_cap_m3_per_d": 80.0
